@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`priceOrder` (src/pricing.ts) passes the gross total to `couponDiscount`; the subtotal after volume
+discounts (`afterVolume`) is already computed and is what the README requires. `Coupons.redeemable`
+compares the date with `validUntil` using `>= 0`, rejecting the last day. `shippingVat` in src/tax.ts
+applies 22%; the receipt prints a "VAT on shipping" row and `vatSummary` in src/invoices.ts adds shipping at
+the standard rate.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** fix both bugs to match the README; make shipping VAT-free consistently in totals, receipt,
+invoice, README.
+
+**Non-Goals:** any other pricing rule; removing `shippingVatCents` from the public types.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Use `sum(afterVolume)` as the coupon base; keep `percentOf` (half-up, integer cents) and `capped`.
+- Change the expiry check to `> 0` (last day included).
+- `shippingVat` returns 0 and `totalCents = goods + shipping + vat`. `shippingVatCents` stays as an always-0
+  field to avoid an API break. Alternative (removing it) rejected as out of scope.
+- Receipt drops the "VAT on shipping" line. Invoice summary adds shipping under rate 0 (net = shipping, VAT 0).
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- The VAT change is a tax-treatment decision requested by a customer; flagged in the proposal for business
+  confirmation.
+- Already placed orders keep their stored totals.
